       EVP_PKEY-HMAC, EVP_KEYMGMT-HMAC, EVP_PKEY-Siphash, EVP_KEYMGMT-Siphash,
       EVP_PKEY-Poly1305, EVP_KEYMGMT-Poly1305, EVP_PKEY-CMAC,
       EVP_KEYMGMT-CMAC - EVP_PKEY legacy MAC keytypes and algorithm support

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The HHMMAACC and CCMMAACC key types are implemented in OpenSSL’s default and
       FIPS providers. Additionally the SSiipphhaasshh and PPoollyy11330055 key types are
       implemented in the default provider. Performing MAC operations via an
       EVP_PKEY is considered legacy and are only available for backwards
       compatibility purposes and for a restricted set of algorithms. The
       preferred way of performing MAC operations is via the EVP_MAC APIs. See
       EEVVPP__MMAACC__iinniitt(3).

       For further details on using EVP_PKEY based MAC keys see
       EEVVPP__SSIIGGNNAATTUURREE--HHMMAACC(7), EEVVPP__SSIIGGNNAATTUURREE--SSiipphhaasshh(7),
       EEVVPP__SSIIGGNNAATTUURREE--PPoollyy11330055(7) or EEVVPP__SSIIGGNNAATTUURREE--CCMMAACC(7).

